{
  "answer": "The country that played the most matches in UEFA European Football Championships, according to the 2024 Guinness World Records, is **Germany** (with 58 matches, achieved between 1960 and 2024) [https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/90527-most-matches-played-in-uefa-european-football-championships-by-a-team].\n\nThe current president of Germany is Frank-Walter Steinmeier, and his current spouse is **Elke Büdenbender** [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elke_B%C3%BCdenbender].",
